Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 00:59:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/19] fix(eval): give the tools three GPUs; DepthPro needs
 12.5 GB per actor

Measured footprints during a blinkdepth run: Molmo fp32 33.0 GB, RoboRefer
18.6 GB, DepthPro 12.5 GB PER ACTOR (two actors = 25 GB), SAM2 1.2 GB each.
That is ~80 GB of tools against the 94.8 GB of two A6000s, i.e. 84% occupancy
with no headroom, so concurrent tool calls (max_parallel_calls=8) OOMed 68
times in 124 samples. The affected samples scored 38.5% against 88.3% for the
clean ones, dragging the benchmark from 88.3% to 83.1%.

Drop EVAL_GPUS to 1 so the tools get three cards, and re-balance the fractional
budget around the measured sizes: Molmo alone on one card, RoboRefer + SAM2 on
another, DepthPro + bbox + grasp on a third. Every upstream replica count is
preserved; only EVAL_GPUS, which is ours to choose, changes. The cost is one
data-parallel policy replica instead of two.

Also enable expandable_segments, which the OOM traces recommend directly.
---
 examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh | 26 ++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh b/examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh
index 2604759e..1f41a061 100755
--- a/examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh
+++ b/examples/toolshed/run_eval.sh
